**Definition 2.1 (The fixed QJM encoder and its decoder variation).** Set
$\alpha_k=2\pi k/3$, $\beta_k=2\pi k/5$, and use the fourteen flags
$F=\{(\mathrm A,k,l):0\le k,l<3\}\sqcup\{(\mathrm B,k):0\le k<5\}$.
Retain the exact QJM data

$$
\begin{aligned}
b_{\mathrm A,k,l}
&=\frac{9w_+(\alpha_k)+\sqrt{119}\,w_-(\alpha_l)}{\sqrt{200}},
&c_{\mathrm A,k,l}&=\frac{400}{1071},\\
a_{\mathrm A,k,l}
&=\frac{1521w_+(\alpha_k)+166\sqrt{119}\,w_-(\alpha_l)}{\sqrt{5592605}},\\
b_{\mathrm B,k}
&=\frac{\sqrt{119}\,d+\sqrt{76}\,w_+(\beta_k)}{\sqrt{195}},
&c_{\mathrm B,k}&=\frac{39}{119},\\
a_{\mathrm B,k}
&=\frac{71\sqrt{119}\,d+94\sqrt{76}\,w_+(\beta_k)}{\sqrt{1271415}}.
\end{aligned}
\tag{2.1}
$$

The circle coefficients are fixed exact algebraic roots-of-unity
values. For $0\le\delta\le1$, put

$$
\begin{gathered}
\sigma_{\mathrm A,k,l,\delta}=a_{\mathrm A,k,l}a_{\mathrm A,k,l}^T,\\
\sigma_{\mathrm B,k,\delta}
=(1-\delta)a_{\mathrm B,k}a_{\mathrm B,k}^T
+\delta w_+(\beta_k)w_+(\beta_k)^T,\\
S_\delta(X)=\sum_fc_f\sigma_{f,\delta}\operatorname{tr}(b_fb_f^TX),
\qquad T_\delta(X)=DS_\delta(D^\dagger XD)D^\dagger.
\end{gathered}
\tag{2.2}
$$

Write $S_Q=S_0$. Its preparation/output row and measurement/input
column populations, in sector order $(0,+,-)$, are the supplied matrix

$$
\Lambda_Q=\begin{pmatrix}
599879/1271415&383116/1271415&0\\
671536/1271415&1280547842618/1422104377215&4626882/5592605\\
0&4464072/5592605&6558328/5592605
\end{pmatrix}.
\tag{2.3}
$$

Define

$$
\begin{gathered}
g=\frac{599879}{1271415},\qquad n=\frac{1+1/r}{2},\qquad
\kappa=\frac{57gn}{238}=\frac{95779(17+r)}{28818740},\\
\Lambda_\delta=\Lambda_Q+
\delta g\begin{pmatrix}-1&-76/119&0\\1&76/119&0\\0&0&0\end{pmatrix}.
\end{gathered}
\tag{2.4}
$$

For every real symmetric $E$, put $t_i=\operatorname{tr}(R_iE)$.
The effect map for the same varied channel is

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathcal A_\delta(E)={}&(\Lambda_\delta)_{00}t_0R_0
+\sum_{j=+,-}\frac{(\Lambda_\delta)_{jj}}8(t_jR_j+2R_jER_j)\\
&+\sum_{i\ne j}\frac{(\Lambda_\delta)_{ij}}{d_id_j}\,t_iR_j\\
&+(1-\delta)\frac{507224}{1271415}(R_0ER_++R_+ER_0)
+\frac{2272374}{5592605}(R_+ER_-+R_-ER_+).
\end{aligned}
\tag{2.5}
$$

Its extension to all complex matrices first takes $(E+E^T)/2$.
The adjoint orientation is $\mathcal A_\delta=S_\delta^\dagger$;
the sector-transfer sum contains $t_iR_j$, not $t_jR_i$.
Thus (1.6), (2.4)–(2.5) specify every singleton and pair residual
of one common channel.

